.TH GIBCERT.SCFG 5
.SH NAME
gibcert.scfg \- configuration file for gibcert
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gibcert.scfg
uses the scfg configuration format. Blocks use braces, directives are
whitespace separated, and values with spaces can be quoted.
.PP
Top-level directives are include, ca, account, provider, challenge, and
certificate.
.SH INCLUDES
.TP
.B include \fIPATH\fR
Load another file, a glob, or a directory. Relative paths are resolved from
the including file. Directory includes load *.scfg files in sorted order.
.SH CA
.TP
.B ca \fINAME\fR { ... }
Define or override a CA profile.
.PP
Directives are:
.TP
.B type acme|local
CA type. Default is acme.
.TP
.B directory \fIURL\fR
ACME directory URL. Required for custom ACME CAs.
.TP
.B common-name \fINAME\fR
Local CA certificate common name.
.TP
.B valid-for \fIDURATION\fR
Local CA certificate validity. Default is 10 years.
.TP
.B key { ... }
Local CA key settings.
.TP
.B persist-identifier \fINAME\fR
CA identifier published in dns-persist-01 standing records. Built in for
letsencrypt and letsencrypt-staging.
.TP
.B profile \fINAME\fR
Default ACME certificate profile to request. Individual certificates may
override it. Advertised profiles are listed by gibcert ca show.
.PP
Built-in ACME profiles are letsencrypt, letsencrypt-staging, zerossl,
google, buypass, and sslcom.
.PP
CA, account, and certificate names are used as directory names under the state
directory. They must be single path components: empty names, ., .., and names
containing / or \e are rejected.
.SH ACCOUNT
.TP
.B account \fINAME\fR { ... }
Define an ACME account.
.PP
Directives are:
.TP
.B ca \fINAME\fR
ACME CA profile. If omitted, the account name is used as the CA name.
.TP
.B email \fIADDRESS\fR
Optional ACME account email contact.
.TP
.B eab { kid \fIKID\fR; hmac-key { file \fIPATH\fR } }
Optional External Account Binding for new account registration. hmac-key
must contain exactly one of file, value, env, command, or systemd-credential.
.TP
.B eab { kid \fIKID\fR; hmac-key { value \fIVALUE\fR } }
Use an inline External Account Binding HMAC key value.
.TP
.B eab { kid \fIKID\fR; hmac-key { env \fINAME\fR } }
Read the External Account Binding HMAC key from an environment variable.
.TP
.B eab { kid \fIKID\fR; hmac-key { command \fIARGV...\fR } }
Run a command without a shell and use stdout as the External Account Binding
HMAC key. Trailing newlines are removed.
.TP
.B eab { kid \fIKID\fR; hmac-key { systemd-credential \fINAME\fR } }
Read the External Account Binding HMAC key from $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/NAME.
.SH PROVIDER
.TP
.B provider \fINAME\fR { ... }
Define a DNS-01 challenge provider.
.PP
Directives are:
.TP
.B type dns
Provider type. Required.
.TP
.B driver \fIDRIVER\fR
DNS driver. Supported values are manual, exec, nsupdate, rfc2136, pdns, and
powerdns.
.TP
.B propagation provider|tool
Whether the provider handles DNS propagation waiting. Default is tool. The
exec driver requires tool because gibdns separates mutation from propagation.
.TP
.B secret \fINAME\fR { file \fIPATH\fR }
Define a secret passed as a file path or read by the driver.
.TP
.B secret \fINAME\fR { value \fIVALUE\fR }
Define an inline secret value.
.TP
.B secret \fINAME\fR { env \fIVAR\fR }
Read a secret value from an environment variable.
.TP
.B secret \fINAME\fR { command \fIARGV...\fR }
Run a command without a shell and use stdout as the secret value. Trailing
newlines are removed.
.TP
.B secret \fINAME\fR { systemd-credential \fINAME\fR }
Read a secret from $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/NAME, for services using systemd
credentials.
.PP
Other provider directives are stored as driver-specific fields.
.SH DNS PROVIDER FIELDS
.SS manual
The manual driver has no required fields.
.SS exec
The exec driver implements the gibdns/draft-01 exec-json binding. It requires:
.TP
.B command \fIARGV...\fR
Execute this argument vector directly for every request. No shell or
protocol-specific argument is added.
.TP
.B zone \fINAME\fR
Optional exact gibdns zone selector. It is required when the provider does not
advertise zone discovery.
.PP
The command reads one gibdns/draft-01 JSON request from standard input and
writes one JSON response to standard output. Diagnostics go to standard error.
The legacy present, cleanup, add-record, and remove-record fields are rejected.
.PP
Other fields become case-sensitive provider.config members. One argument is a
JSON string and multiple arguments are an array of strings. gibcert resolves
all configured secret sources and sends their values in provider.secrets on
standard input; capability requests omit secrets. No DNSREC environment
variables are exported.
.PP
The provider must implement capabilities and rrset.patch. It must advertise
concurrent-safe patching or provide rrset.get with if_revision and if_absent.
The exec driver always uses gibcert's authoritative propagation check.
.SS rfc2136 and nsupdate
Fields are:
.TP
.B command \fIPATH\fR
nsupdate executable. Default is nsupdate.
.TP
.B server \fIADDRESS\fR
Optional server line in the nsupdate script.
.TP
.B zone \fINAME\fR
Optional zone line in the nsupdate script.
.PP
The first secret with a file value is passed to nsupdate with -k.
.SS powerdns and pdns
Fields are:
.TP
.B api-url \fIURL\fR
Base PowerDNS API URL. Required.
.TP
.B server-id \fIID\fR
PowerDNS server id. Default is localhost.
.TP
.B ttl \fISECONDS\fR
TXT record TTL. Default is 60.
.PP
The api-key secret is required. The zone is detected automatically by listing
zones on the server and choosing the longest suffix match for the challenge
FQDN.
.SH TOP-LEVEL CHALLENGE
.TP
.B challenge http-01 { webroot \fIPATH\fR }
Set a global HTTP-01 challenge default using an external web server's webroot.
.TP
.B challenge http-01 { listen \fIADDR\fR }
Set a global HTTP-01 challenge default using gibcert's built-in standalone
HTTP server. Mutually exclusive with webroot.
.SH GROUP
.TP
.B group \fINAME\fR { ... }
Define a named bundle of certificate settings that certificates inherit via
.B groups.
A group may set
.BR account ,
.BR ca ,
.BR profile ,
.BR preferred-chain ,
.BR valid-for ,
.BR key ,
.BR challenge ,
.BR renew ,
.BR deploy ,
and
.BR reload .
It cannot set
.B names
and cannot reference other groups.
.PP
When a certificate lists groups, scalar settings set on the certificate replace
the group's, while unset ones are inherited; it is an error for two listed
groups to set the same scalar. Deploy blocks are merged by name: a certificate
deploy overrides only the fields it sets on an inherited deploy of the same name,
and a new name is added alongside the inherited ones.
.PP
Deploy target paths
.RB ( cert ,
.BR chain ,
.BR fullchain ,
.BR key ,
.BR cert-der ,
.BR key-der )
may contain the placeholders
.B {cert}
(the certificate's block name) and
.B {name}
(its first subject name), which expand per certificate. Templating applies to
all certificates, not only grouped ones; hook commands and ownership fields are
never templated. An unknown placeholder is an error.
.SH CERTIFICATE
.TP
.B certificate \fINAME\fR { ... }
Define one managed certificate.
.PP
Directives are:
.TP
.B account \fINAME\fR
ACME account to use. Mutually exclusive with ca.
.TP
.B ca \fINAME\fR
CA profile to use. For ACME CAs, gibcert uses an implicit account named
ca:<ca-name>. For local CAs, gibcert signs locally. Mutually exclusive with
account.
.TP
.B groups \fINAME\fR...
Inherit settings from one or more
.B group
blocks. See
.B GROUP.
.TP
.B requires \fINAME\fR...
Other certificates that must run before this one; this certificate is skipped if
any of them fails. See
.B DEPENDENCIES.
.TP
.B wants \fINAME\fR...
Other certificates that should run before this one, without gating. See
.B DEPENDENCIES.
.TP
.B names \fINAME\fR...
Subject names. Required. A name that parses as an IP address is requested as
an IP identifier (RFC 8738); IP identifiers require the http-01 or
tls-alpn-01 challenge.
.TP
.B valid-for \fIDURATION\fR
Local CA certificate validity. Default is 90 days. Only valid with a local CA.
.TP
.B preferred-chain \fINAME\fR
Prefer an ACME certificate chain whose final certificate subject or issuer
matches \fINAME\fR, for example ISRG Root X1. If the default chain does not
match, gibcert fetches alternate chains offered by the ACME server. Issuance
fails if no offered chain matches. Only valid with ACME certificates.
.TP
.B profile \fINAME\fR
ACME certificate profile to request for this certificate. Overrides the
profile set on the CA. Only valid with ACME certificates.
.TP
.B key { ... }
Certificate key settings.
.TP
.B challenge \fITYPE\fR { ... }
ACME challenge settings. Supported types are http-01, dns-01, tls-alpn-01,
and dns-persist-01.
.TP
.B renew { before-expiry \fIDURATION\fR }
Renewal window. If unset, gibcert uses one third of the current certificate
lifetime, capped at 30 days.
.TP
.B deploy \fINAME\fR { ... }
Deployment target. Optional; a certificate with no deploy blocks is still
issued and stored under the state directory, but no files are written
elsewhere.
.TP
.B reload \fICOMMAND\fR
Command run once per apply/renew run when any deploy on this certificate
changed. Identical commands across certificates are coalesced into a single
invocation. Repeatable. See
.B RELOAD HOOKS
in
.BR gibcert (1)
hook documentation.
.TP
.B tlsa { ... }
Manage DANE TLSA records for the certificate. Optional.
.TP
.B failover { ... }
Alternate ACME issuers tried when the primary issuer cannot issue. Optional.
Only valid for ACME certificates. See
.B FAILOVER.
.SH FAILOVER
.B failover { ... }
lists alternate issuers tried, in order, when the certificate's primary issuer
(its
.B account
or
.B ca)
cannot issue \(em for example during a CA outage, a rate-limit, or when the
requested profile is unavailable. Each child line is one issuer:
.TP
.B account \fINAME\fR
Use an explicit ACME account.
.TP
.B ca \fINAME\fR
Use the CA's implicit "ca:<name>" account.
.PP
The two forms may be mixed. The primary issuer is always attempted first; a
failover is only reached when every preceding issuer fails, so a healthy primary
is never skipped and gibcert returns to it on the next run. Failover triggers on
any issuance failure. If every issuer fails, issuance fails and the error
reports each issuer's failure. Each entry must reference an ACME account or ACME
CA and must differ from the primary and from the other entries.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B requires
and
.B wants
order certificates relative to one another, modelled on systemd's
.B Requires=
and
.B Wants=.
Both make the named certificates run before this one.
.B requires
also gates: if a required certificate fails or is itself skipped during the run,
this certificate is skipped \(em not issued and not deployed.
.B wants
is advisory ordering only.
.PP
Dependencies apply to
.B gibcert apply
and
.B gibcert renew,
which process certificates in dependency order; they are not pulled into
single-certificate commands such as
.B gibcert issue.
In
.B renew,
a required certificate that is already valid (and so not renewed this run)
counts as satisfied; gating only triggers when a required certificate is
processed and fails. Each name must reference another certificate; a certificate
cannot depend on itself, repeat a name, or list a name in both
.B requires
and
.B wants,
and the graph must be acyclic.
.SH KEY
.TP
.B type ecdsa|rsa
Key type. Default is ecdsa.
.TP
.B curve p256|p384
ECDSA curve. Default is p256.
.TP
.B bits 2048|3072|4096
RSA key size.
.TP
.B reuse
Reuse an existing certificate key on renewal. Only valid for certificate
keys.
.SH CERTIFICATE CHALLENGE
.TP
.B challenge http-01 { webroot \fIPATH\fR }
Use HTTP-01 with the given webroot. The webroot may come from the global
challenge block.
.TP
.B challenge http-01 { listen \fIADDR\fR }
Use HTTP-01 with gibcert's built-in standalone HTTP server on the given
bind address. Mutually exclusive with webroot. Binding privileged ports
requires root or CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE.
.TP
.B challenge tls-alpn-01 { listen \fIADDR\fR }
Use TLS-ALPN-01 with gibcert's built-in standalone TLS listener on the given
bind address. Required for tls-alpn-01.
.TP
.B challenge dns-01 { provider \fINAME\fR [propagation-timeout \fIDURATION\fR] [alias-fqdn \fIFQDN\fR | alias-domain \fIDOMAIN\fR] }
Use DNS-01 with the named provider. The default propagation timeout is 120s.
With alias-fqdn, gibcert publishes the TXT record at the given exact FQDN.
With alias-domain, gibcert publishes at _acme-challenge.<domain>.<alias-domain>.
.TP
.B challenge dns-persist-01 { [provider \fINAME\fR] [alias-fqdn \fIFQDN\fR | alias-domain \fIDOMAIN\fR] }
Use the dns-persist-01 standing-record challenge. The provider is only used by
gibcert dns-persist install; renewals never write DNS. Wildcard names require a
standing record with policy=wildcard.
.SH DEPLOY
.TP
.B deploy \fINAME\fR { ... }
Copy stored certificate material to service paths.
.PP
Directives are:
.TP
.B cert \fIPATH\fR
Leaf certificate destination.
.TP
.B chain \fIPATH\fR
Issuer chain destination.
.TP
.B fullchain \fIPATH\fR
Leaf plus issuer chain destination.
.TP
.B key \fIPATH\fR
Private key destination.
.TP
.B cert-der \fIPATH\fR
Leaf certificate destination in binary DER, for trust stores that expect DER.
.TP
.B key-der \fIPATH\fR
Private key destination in binary DER (the on-disk PKCS#8 encoding, unarmored).
.TP
.B owner \fINAME\fR
Owner for deployed files.
.TP
.B group \fINAME\fR
Group for deployed files.
.TP
.B mode \fIMODE\fR
File mode for deployed files. Must be 0777 or lower.
.TP
.B before \fICOMMAND\fR
Command to run through the platform shell before changed material is deployed.
.TP
.B after \fICOMMAND\fR
Command to run through the platform shell after changed material is deployed.
.PP
At least one of cert, chain, fullchain, key, cert-der, or key-der must be set.
All deploy paths must be absolute.
.SH TLSA
.TP
.B tlsa { ... }
Manage DANE TLSA records for the certificate. Directives are:
.TP
.B provider \fINAME\fR
DNS provider used to publish and remove TLSA records. Required. Must use a
driver that supports persistent record edits: exec, nsupdate, rfc2136, pdns,
or powerdns.
.TP
.B port \fIPORT\fR[/\fIPROTO\fR]
Repeatable. Port and transport for which TLSA records are published.
Protocol defaults to tcp; tcp, udp, and sctp are accepted.
.TP
.B ttl \fISECONDS\fR
TLSA record TTL. Default is 3600. Must be less than the certificate renewal
window.
.TP
.B type \fIUSAGE\fR \fISELECTOR\fR \fIMTYPE\fR
Certificate usage, selector, and matching type. Default is 3 1 1 (DANE-EE,
SPKI, SHA-256). Only DANE-EE with SPKI selector is supported. Matching type
must be 1 (SHA-256) or 2 (SHA-512).
.PP
For TLSA-managed certificates gibcert keeps two private keys at all times:
privkey.pem (live) and privkey-next.pem (staged). The staged key's TLSA
fingerprint is pre-published in DNS. When the next renewal is due and the
staged TLSA has propagated for more than ttl, gibcert issues against the
staged key, promotes it, generates a new staged next-key, and publishes its
TLSA. The retired key's TLSA is removed.
.SH DURATIONS
Expiry-related fields accept Go duration syntax or an integer day suffix such
as 30d. Other duration fields use Go duration syntax such as 120s or 5m.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
account letsencrypt {
  ca letsencrypt
  email admin@example.com
}

challenge http-01 {
  webroot /var/www/acme-challenge
}

certificate example.com {
  account letsencrypt
  names example.com www.example.com

  deploy nginx {
    fullchain /etc/nginx/tls/example.com/fullchain.pem
    key /etc/nginx/tls/example.com/privkey.pem
    owner root
    group www-data
    mode 0640
    after "systemctl reload nginx"
  }
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gibcert (1)
